{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784617772,"nonce":"9HrrrwUGMZvFxEd58//eHmbDy7s=","title":"The server's generated `openapi.json` (utoipa) ships with empty operation","message":"`tags` and no top-level `tags`. `starlight-openapi` in the docs site builds its\nper-operation pages and sidebar groups from tags, so an untagged spec rendered\nonly a bare overview (no operation pages).\n\nAs a docs-side workaround, `ui/scarab-docs-ui/scripts/gen-openapi.mjs` now\nderives a tag per operation from its path and writes a gitignored tagged copy\nthat the plugin consumes.\n\nProper fix\nTag operations at the source — add `tags` to the utoipa `#[utoipa::path(...)]`\nannotations (or via a modifier) in `crates/scarab-server` so the canonical spec\ncarries real, curated groups. Once the source spec has tags, the docs\n`gen:openapi` step + `openapi.gen.json` schema indirection can be removed\n(revert astro.config.mjs `schema` back to `../../openapi.json`).\n\nEvidence\n- Current ops have `tags: []` (no top-level `tags`).\n- Docs workaround: `ui/scarab-docs-ui/scripts/gen-openapi.mjs`.\n- Groups currently derived = Runs / Repositories / Environments / Secrets /\n  Webhooks / Auth \u0026 Identity / System.","files":null}]}